{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "id": "gen-061",
   "subject": "Adjusting staff permission tiers for financial data",
   "body": "Hello, I am reviewing our current user access settings and would like to set up some custom security roles for our administrative team. We need to make sure that front desk staff cannot view sensitive payroll and financial records while still retaining scheduling access. Could someone walk me through the best way to structure these permission levels in our enterprise account? Thank you."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-062",
   "subject": "Incorrect subscription charge on recent invoice",
   "body": "Hi there, I am terribly sorry to bother you with this, but I noticed our latest monthly software subscription invoice has a duplicate charge on it. We are only a solo practice and should not be billed twice for the professional tier. Could you please look into our account history and issue a refund for the extra amount? I appreciate your help."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-063",
   "subject": "Attaching outside lab documents",
   "body": "Hello, I am trying to figure out how to upload scanned paper lab reports into patient charts. I cannot seem to find where the upload button went after the last update. Can you point me in the right direction?"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-064",
   "subject": "Password reset policies and staff account lockout issues",
   "body": "Good morning, I am writing because I am a bit confused about how our practice is supposed to handle staff password resets and overall security policies. Yesterday, two of our part-time staff members got locked out of their accounts after trying to log in, and when I went to the admin panel to reset their credentials, I couldn't find where to adjust the lockout duration or complexity requirements. We are on the essentials plan, and I want to make sure we are compliant without making it impossible for everyone to sign in. Could someone please explain where these settings are hidden and how I can update our practice-wide policy?"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-065",
   "subject": "Lab value critical flags not triggering correctly",
   "body": "I'm really frustrated because the system keeps missing abnormal flags for critical lab results on my patients. I tried updating the threshold parameters in my settings yesterday, but incoming labs are still not auto-flagging the way they should. This is a major safety concern for my solo practice, so please let me know how to fix this immediately."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-066",
   "subject": "Publishing digital intake questionnaires",
   "body": "Dear support team, please provide instructions on how to publish our new custom patient intake forms for online completion prior to visits. Thank you."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-067",
   "subject": "Pharmacy directory search completely down",
   "body": "This is ridiculous. None of our medical assistants can look up pharmacies in the directory right now, and we are completely stuck trying to send out prescriptions for patients. The entire pharmacy search module seems to be frozen or throwing a server error across all our workstations. We cannot work normally like this. Fix this outage immediately!"
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-068",
   "subject": "EPCS token authentication failure",
   "body": "My two-factor authentication token keeps failing when I try to sign controlled substance prescriptions. I completed identity proofing last week, but now the signing window errors out every time. Please resolve this so I can finish my queue."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-069",
   "subject": "Assistance needed with medication out-of-stock workflows and therapeutic alternatives",
   "body": "Hello support team, I hope you are having a productive week. I am reaching out on behalf of our clinical providers here at the large clinic regarding how we manage out-of-stock medication alerts. Lately, we have received a high volume of pharmacy notices indicating that certain drugs are unavailable, and our staff is stumbling a bit on the best way to route substitution requests through the messaging workflows. Could you please provide a detailed walkthrough or documentation on how to efficiently switch these prescriptions to alternative therapeutic agents without losing the audit trail? We want to ensure our workflow remains seamless. Thank you so much for your time and assistance."
  },
  {
   "id": "gen-070",
   "subject": "Guidance on medication substitution messaging workflows",
   "body": "Good afternoon. As a solo practitioner utilizing the enterprise tier, I am writing to request guidance on handling out-of-stock medication alerts and processing therapeutic substitutions through our current messaging framework. Kindly provide documentation or best practices for updating pharmacy substitution notifications efficiently. Thank you for your assistance."
  }
 ]
}
